From b2e4dd25d724fa191c5e278cc80bb13f81de7e22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:57:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PlaitOS: Snapseed-style editor (Looks, Tools, Export; Tune
 image)

- Three tabs instead of five: Looks (filters), Tools (a grid of every tool
  in Adjust, Shape and Create groups) and Export (export and print, moved
  out of the overflow menu). Frames and Effects open their strips from the
  grid; Tools again returns to it
- Tune image: Exposure, Contrast, Saturation, Vibrance, Highlights,
  Shadows and Hue in one tool. No slider: drag the photo sideways to
  adjust, up or down to pick from a list over the photo; a pill shows the
  value with a centre-zero bar (double-tap it to reset). Tool bar: cancel,
  the list, hold to compare, apply. Cancel undoes the whole visit
- Drags in a tool no longer unveil the original (compare is the button or
  a long press)
- Tool rows draw tonal tiles with Material Symbols, filters and frames
  rounded previews with an accent ring; the tool panel is restyled (tinted
  slider, round tonal cancel/apply, sentence case)
- Sliders open at their neutral value (Exposure opened at +50)
- No duplicate menus: the shortcut tool row inside a tool is gone
- versionCode 40057

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017VXjYUWzBqMCeUoJD2Suc4
